    "narrative": "For today\u2019s slate on July 16, 2026, the **Austin Waves** offense faces a challenging landscape, with our primary spark plugs sidelined by team off-days or injury. With **Kyle Tucker**, **Gunnar Henderson**, and **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** all inactive, we are forced to lean on depth pieces to navigate a rotation of mediocre matchups. **Jorge Polanco** remains our most viable starter at 50.85; while Nola presents a firm test, **Jorge Polanco**\u2019s park-adjusted projections benefit from a slight boost, though his efficiency is hampered by the current R/R platoon disadvantage. We are also monitoring **Jackson Merrill** and **Heliot Ramos**, whose sprint speed profiles remain critical for our SB-heavy strategy; if they can successfully exploit the gaps against their respective starters, they provide the best pathway to exceeding their marginal efficiency scores.\n\nThe bench remains crowded with prospects and utility fillers, but **Nasim Nunez** arguably came the closest to a start today. His elite sprint speed makes him a perpetual candidate for a late-game stolen base attempt, yet his raw hitting profile struggled to overcome the baseline projection against today's projected pitching talent. We are exercising caution with **Luis Robert Jr.**, who remains on the IL, and we continue to prioritize the development of **Coby Mayo** and **Josh Jung** on our reserve bench, keeping them ready for when favorable park factors align. Be advised that with **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** and **Jordan Westburg** navigating volatile matchups, the risk of a sub-40 performance is non-zero; we are prioritizing game caps, opting to bench the likes of **Sam Antonacci** and **Brayan Rocchio** to ensure we don't bleed points on high-risk, low-reward outcomes.",
